In silico Classification of Manganese/Iron Superoxide Dismutase Protein
Sequences across Coral Host and Symbiont Species

Abstract

SOD2, or Mn/FeSOD, is important blah blah. Across XXX species of corals and YYY
species of symbiotic algae, Mn/FeSOD like protein sequences can be categorized
into four categories and an additional, putative, weakly supported fifth
category. This paper outlines genomic and transcriptomic evidence (using
submitted and public datasets) for these categories, presents HMM profiles for
each category, and reviews functional studies for each type of proteins in
existing literature.

Introduction

We found all K04564 matched gene model derived, HMM searched, or RNAseq derived
sequences, filtered them through a set of rules that checked key residues, then
looked upstream for possible M / start sites and ran the sequences through
DeepLoc. For SP and mTP, we limited M to XXX upstream of PF00081. For SP_cTP,
we limited M to XXX upstream of PF00081. It’s possible there’s a different
architecture with an M that’s not in these ranges, this paper does not address
that.

